The `findGCD` method is used to find the greatest common divisor of two positive integers using the Euclidean algorithm. This algorithm calculates the remainder of dividing the larger number by the smaller number and continues until the remainder is zero. The last non-zero remainder is the greatest common divisor of the two numbers.

The `main` method uses these two methods to prompt the user to enter two positive integers, validate the input, find their greatest common divisor using the Euclidean algorithm, and output the result.

